  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Some additional severe storms and flash flooding\nwill be possible Wednesday. Wednesday's severe weather and \nflooding threat is not expected to be as widespread though as it\nwill be confined mainly to areas south and east of the urban \ncorridor.\n\nOn Wednesday, the cold front will sag farther south and east and \ndepending on how quickly this clears our area there will be some \nshowers and thunderstorms, especially as additional shortwaves move \nthrough the flow within the upper-level trough overhead. This looks \nto be more concentrated across southern New Jersey to Delmarva but \ncould extend into the I-95 corridor for a time. There is some severe \nweather risk mainly south/east of the I-95 corridor with locally \ndamaging wind gusts the main threat. The greater instability and \nshear looks to reside across Delmarva on southward, where a little \nhigher severe thunderstorm risk is indicated. Some locally excessive \nrainfall is possible with some local flash flood risk, however this \nlooks to be less compared to today given the shift farther south and \nmore into the coastal plain. Once the front moves away by later \nWednesday, it turns drier for Thursday/Friday and right into the \nweekend.",
